*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
*** Title: Deprivation items, household structure and robustness (IWP Employees vs. AROP w/o IWP)
*** Aim: All calculations behind the deprivation statements of the paper (cf. SA2 presentation / working document)
***   PART A: Setup - 13 SMSD items (+ 3 arrears sub-items), samples, survey design, helper program
***   PART B: Descriptives - item prevalence by group (pp difference, relative change, ratio), by year
***   PART C: Headline SMD effect - M1 year FE, M2-M10 year FE + one control each, M11 all controls
***   PART D: Time pattern - SMD by year and group
***   PART E: Item decomposition - effect of employment on each item (M1-M11), Holm/Bonferroni-adjusted p-values
***   PART F: Heterogeneity - group x household type / children (Wald tests, Holm-adjusted), AMEs by household type
***   PART G: Household structure and poverty risk - children vs. adults (M1-M4), pre and post, per group; test children = adults
***   PART H: Sector within IWP Employees - IWP rate and SMD by sector (sector exists only for persons with a job)
*** Groups: smd_grp (script 03): 1 = IWP Employees, 0 = AROP w/o IWP; both 18-64, post-transfer, without old-age benefit recipients
*** Outcome: smd = RX060 as provided in the UDB
*** Survey design: svyset hh_cl [pw=dwt] (household cluster, idhh unique within year)
*** Effects reported as OR and as average predicted shares (margins) with pp difference and relative change in %
*** Input: SILC_All_Years_Adjusted.dta (script 03)
*** Output: 05_Deprivation_log.txt, 05_Deprivation_Results.xlsx (one sheet per part)
*** Requires: Stata 17 or newer
*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

